<?xml version="1.0"?>
<!-- Unitree G1, 12 leg joints (pelvis floating; waist, arms and head on fixed joints).
     From unitreerobotics/unitree_rl_gym, resources/robots/g1_description/g1_12dof.urdf
     (BSD 3-Clause, Copyright Unitree Robotics; see LICENSE in this folder).
     Changed for crucible (masses, inertias, joints and limits are unchanged):
       * removed <visual> elements (the meshes are in g1_12dof.cmesh); replaced the
         <mujoco> tag with our standard one (keep every body as written, no inertia changes)
       * collision (tools/unitree_to_assets.py): each collision mesh became one cylinder
         fitted to it (crucible reads cylinders as capsules); Unitree's shoulder
         cylinders kept; logo_link none; the 4 foot spheres per ankle_roll_link
         (radius 5 mm) kept: the only spheres (the tasks take them as the feet) -->
